1.0beta6

* Fix sinh_rd, sinh_ru and sinh_rz at x = +-710.475860073944, where
  they returned +-inf instead of +-the largest double.
* Fix atanpi_rd, atanpi_ru and atanpi_rz for finite |x| >= 2^54, where
  they returned +-1/2.
* Fix atanpi_ru(1) and atanpi_rd(-1), which returned the double next
  to +-1/4 instead of +-1/4.
* Stop counting calls to the accurate step in a global variable, which
  was not safe when several threads call crlibm.
* Fix asin, acos, asinpi and acospi for |x| >= 0.75, where they could
  round to the wrong neighbour, and the directed modes could return a
  value on the wrong side of the exact result.
* Fix asinpi_rd and asinpi_ru for negative x, where they could round
  toward zero instead of down or up.
* Fix sinpi and tanpi for 2^-1000 <= |x| < 2^-950, where they could
  round to the wrong neighbour, and the directed modes could return a
  value on the wrong side of the exact result.
* Fix tanpi_rd and tanpi_rz for |x| just below 2^-31, where they could
  be one ulp off, and tanpi_rd could return a value above the exact
  result.
* tanpi(n + 1/2) now returns +inf for even n and -inf for odd n, as
  documented, instead of NaN.
* sinpi and cospi now return the signed zeros given in the
  documentation, in all rounding modes: sinpi(x) is 0 with the sign of
  x for integer x, and cospi(x) is +0 for x an integer plus 1/2.
  Before, sinpi_rd returned -0 and sinpi_ru +0 for |x| < 2^52, and
  cospi_rd returned -0.
* Fix asin_rd, asin_ru and asin_rz at x = -0.478107559539333, the
  negative of the hardest case of asin, which was handled only for
  x > 0. asin_rd returned a value above the exact result.
* Fix acos_ru(6.123233995736766e-17), which returned the double above
  the correctly rounded result.
* Fix the conversion of multiple-precision numbers to subnormal doubles
  in the directed modes. No function returned a wrong result because of
  it.
* Use the portable log by default. --enable-double-extended builds
  log-de.c as before.
* Use SSE2 arithmetic by default on 32-bit x86. The x87 arithmetic
  used before computes in extended precision, which breaks the exact
  operations crlibm relies on, and gave wrong results in the directed
  modes. --disable-sse2 builds as before.
* Compile with -ffp-contract=off.
* Fix the build of crlibm_exit without fpu_control.h.
